<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25992" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lātĭfundĭum</span></b> ,
			ii, n.
		1. latus-fundus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a large landed property, large estate</i> or <i>farm</i> (not ante-Aug.), <i><span class="en">Plin. 18, 6,
				7, § 35</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nisi latifundiis vestris maria cinxistis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 89, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">metiri me geometres docet latifundia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 88, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">possidere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 77</span></i>
			.</div>
